"""Mutations of the rigid body (src/game/rigid_body.cpp, part 5a: lifetime, setup, state, impulses,
saved games and the per-frame bookkeeping) for ../mutfast.py with the rigid body build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_rigid_body.py --models DIR --build build_rigid.bat --check check_rigid.py

Each should make check_rigid.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Left out as equivalent:
LengthOf's exact-1 branch (a square within 1e-8 of 1 is 1), NormalizeBy's unit early out (the
scale is then 1), Topple's `* 0.0f +` (a finite sum times 0 adds nothing), Tick's centre update
when an actor moved (RefreshMatrices sets it again before Tick returns), Step's `time > 83` (83
gives the same scale and time), the destructor's contact release (memory only) and the save
record's w-less copies.

Surviving (2026-10-25, 5 of 399): "setup x vs y", "setup y vs z", "setup x vs z" are equivalent
(two equal sides: when they are the longest the longest-to-middle factor is 1 either way, else
both branches make the same call); "normalize sign x" is not reached in part 5a (an axis or push
under 1e-4 long); "topple axis order" changes an axis's last bit at most, which the push's own
normalisation absorbed in every case tried."""
